      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 36,
      "english": {
        "kind": "published",
        "text": "In the ninth yanxi year [166 CE], during the reign of Emperor Huan, the king of Da Qin (the Roman Empire), Andun (Marcus Aurelius Antoninus), sent envoys from beyond the frontiers through Rinan (Commandery on the central Vietnamese coast), to offer elephant tusks, rhinoceros horn, and turtle shell. This was the very first time there was [direct] communication [between the two countries]. The tribute brought was neither precious nor rare, raising suspicion that the accounts [of the 'envoys'] might be exaggerated.",
        "ground": "index",
        "attribution": "John E. Hill, '\"Chapter on the Western Regions\" from Hou Hanshu 88', draft annotated translation, University of Washington Silk Road Seattle project.",
