      "region": "Southeast Asia",
      "citation": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%93c_Eo",
      "source_field": "original_text_excerpt",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 398,
      "english": {
        "kind": "source",
        "text": "The remains found at Oc Eo include pottery, tools, jewelry, casts for making jewelry, coins, and religious statues. Among the finds are gold jewellery imitating coins from the Roman Empire of the Antonine period... Oc Eo was near Chinese-controlled Jiaozhou and the region where Chinese historical texts claim the Romans first landed before venturing further into China to conduct diplomacy in 166.",
